cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "VectorDB Proof: MongoDB $vectorSearch vs Qdrant on a 16 GB laptop"
message: If you use this protocol or results, please cite this repository.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Deepak
    website: https://github.com/drakeRAGE
date-released: "2026-09-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/drakeRAGE/mongo-vs-qdrant-local
url: https://github.com/drakeRAGE/mongo-vs-qdrant-local
abstract: >-
  Reproducible local study of when a dedicated vector database (Qdrant)
  is preferable to MongoDB Community $vectorSearch (mongod + mongot).
  Frozen BGE-small 384-d embeddings, iso-config and iso-recall protocol,
  measured through 500K vectors on a 16 GB Windows laptop.
keywords:
  - vector search
  - HNSW
  - MongoDB
  - Qdrant
  - benchmark
  - recall
